[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
[b]Mid-mission saves in coop.[/b] Vanilla coop has no saving at all: if the mission goes wrong you start over. This mod adds two buttons to the [b]reinforcement panel[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]Save[/b]: every PC saves the current battle state at the same simulation step. A new checkpoint overwrites the previous one, and the mission's own autosaves become checkpoints too.[/*]
[*][b]Reload[/b]: the host's game leaves the match and starts the same mission again automatically, and every PC loads the checkpoint instead of the mission start, with units, triggers and objectives restored.[/*]
[/list]Checkpoints live only for the current mission session: they're meant for "retry from here", not for saving and continuing another day.

[b]Every player in the match needs it[/b]: the DLL [b]and[/b] the [i]coop_checkpoint[/i] data mod enabled (the mod list must match anyway to join). The buttons appear only in multiplayer; single-player missions are left as they are.

[size=4][b]Upgrading from a version before 1.0.2[/b][/size]
Up to 1.0.1 the data mod shipped its own copy of every mission. Extracting 1.0.2 over it leaves those old copies in place, and they hide the missions of other mods (for example a skirmish doctrine mod). Every player of the coop match has to do this once:
[list=1]
[*]Close the game.[/*]
[*]Delete the folder [i]<game>\mods\coop_checkpoint[/i].[/*]
[*]Extract the new zip into the game folder and overwrite.[/*]
[*]Start the game and check that [b]coop_checkpoint[/b] is still enabled in [i]Options > Mods[/i].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the zip from the Files tab.[/*]
[*]Extract it into the game folder, the one that contains [b]binaries[/b] and [b]mods[/b], e.g. [i]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Call to Arms - Gates of Hell[/i]. If Windows asks, overwrite [b]version.dll[/b]: it's the same file in all my mods.[/*]
[*]Start the game and enable [b]coop_checkpoint[/b] in [i]Options > Mods[/i].[/*]
[/list]After installing you should have:
[code]<game>\binaries\x64\version.dll
<game>\binaries\x64\goh_mods\coop_checkpoint.dll
<game>\mods\coop_checkpoint\[/code][b]Uninstall:[/b] disable or delete [i]mods\coop_checkpoint[/i] and delete [i]binaries\x64\goh_mods\coop_checkpoint.dll[/i]. If you have none of my other mods installed, also delete [i]binaries\x64\version.dll[/i] and the [i]goh_mods[/i] folder.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Works in campaign and skirmish missions played in coop, including missions replaced by other mods, in any mod-list order.[/*]
[*][b]Save[/b] button (10 s cooldown): every PC, including the host's local server, saves at the same point of the simulation.[/*]
[*][b]Reload[/b] button: any player can press it. After about 2 s the host's game leaves the match, waits for the lobby and starts the same mission again, then every PC loads its own checkpoint.[/*]
[*]The mission's own autosaves become checkpoints too.[/*]
[*]The game files on disk are never modified: the DLL adds the buttons to each mission in memory while the game reads it. The data mod only holds the button icons and texts.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Call to Arms - Gates of Hell: Ostfront, x64, tested on game version [b]1.067.0[/b].[/*]
[*]No other mods needed. The mod loader ([b]version.dll[/b]) and the [i]coop_checkpoint[/i] data mod are included in the zip.[/*]
[*]All players need the same DLL version and the data mod enabled.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]A script sequence that was halfway through when the checkpoint was saved doesn't resume after a reload.[/*]
[*]Checkpoints are session-only: the files stay on disk ([i]Documents\My Games\gates of hell\profiles\<id>\save\coop_ckpt.sav[/i]), but loading them is only automatic through [b]Reload[/b] in the same mission.[/*]
[*]Loading a big mission after a reload can take 10-15 s.[/*]
[*]Unit re-assignement is random.[/*]
[/list]Troubleshooting logs: [i]%TEMP%\goh_coop_checkpoint_call_to_arms.exe.log[/i] and [i]%TEMP%\goh_coop_checkpoint_call_to_arms_server.exe.log[/i]

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
Open source: the DLL is written in C and the data mod (icons and texts) is generated by a script. Source, build instructions and my other Gates of Hell mods (Coop Game Speed, Loot Highlight, Inspect Preview): [url=https://github.com/nicko996/goh-coop-mods]github.com/nicko996/goh-coop-mods[/url]

